From: MPLAPACK maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Canonical +0 for cu_freal zero arithmetic results

Base: mpc_cuda abd9407; independent of the correctly-rounded div/sqrt patch.
cu_freal has no signed zero. Handle both zero inputs before returning operands,
do not negate a zero subtrahend, and canonicalize zero in neg/abs/scale2.
Nonzero results and signatures are unchanged. MPFR oracle zero results are
canonicalized; signed-zero consumers must retain their own sign policy.
Standalone host/device tests are in tools/test_fzero.cpp (or its .cu wrapper),
with a frozen pre-fix oracle for every nonzero result. Build with the include/
search path and -lmpfr -lgmp. No upstream PR has been submitted.

